From c77037a4c9b543f36aedf7d16d8ec22ffc74acc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:14:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(state): online FTS plan judges integrity_check past the
 old 100k cap

The online stale-FTS plan collected integrity_check output into a list capped at
100,000 lines and refused any check that reached the cap as an unfinished walk.
A family the plan detaches leaves its pages orphaned ("Page N: never used", one
line per page): an example recovery left more orphaned pages than the cap, so every
later plan was repeatedly refused with fts_stale set.

- plan_from_check judges each line as it arrives and keeps only a count, the
  damaged families and the refusing line; plan_online_recovery iterates each
  row's text lazily (the b-tree walk is one newline-joined row) instead of
  splitting it into a list
- the cap rises to 5,000,000 lines: far below SQLITE_MAX_LENGTH, above which
  SQLite drops the walk text and the check returns no rows at all
- a check that returned no line is refused (never read as a clean store)
- the per-line structural test is factored out of integrity_damage_is_structural

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
